Three more seeds

• Naturity. A ruler measures everyone’s maturity by the height they’ve reached. A gardener records how long each plant has spent putting down roots. Tell three skits about one festival and change the measurement in the final scene.
• The choir with one lantern. Four singers take 1, 2, 7, and 10 minutes to cross a bridge. Two may cross at a time and the slower person sets the pace. The fastest singer volunteers to escort everyone. How do the two slow singers cut the total to 17 minutes? Give the returns a refrain.
• The house of two wallpapers. Two sisters draw conjugate maps of a kitchen from opposite sides of a mirror. Let each recognize one feature the other misreads. Give them a decision that requires knowing what the maps share and where their orientations differ.